77
00:04:57,014 --> 00:05:00,226
The flag is not even the nearest
change that caused the outage.

78
00:05:01,144 --> 00:05:03,921
This still does not establish
the cause of the problem.

79
00:05:04,597 --> 00:05:09,102
It does establish ordering and gives
any agent a bounded search window.

80
00:05:10,022 --> 00:05:15,147
Source type and observation time
remain attached, so a rollout event

81
00:05:15,255 --> 00:05:19,328
cannot be confused with telemetry
or with a larger operator action

82
00:05:21,256 --> 00:05:24,793
So if we can talk further on the
architecture, what an evidence-first

83
00:05:24,833 --> 00:05:26,333
architecture would look like.

84
00:05:26,984 --> 00:05:31,327
So this is the broader Beacon
architecture in one short view.

85
00:05:32,196 --> 00:05:36,297
Metrics, logs, Kubernetes and
deployment state, repository

86
00:05:36,297 --> 00:05:37,640
history, and feature flags.

87
00:05:38,092 --> 00:05:43,024
These are all the live signals that
you get for a given incident, and

88
00:05:43,025 --> 00:05:48,111
they become type evidence by, by
kind of aggregating everything,

89
00:05:48,135 --> 00:05:50,059
