that could disprove a hypothesis.

94
00:06:06,977 --> 00:06:09,707
Why is missing evidence
very important in this?

95
00:06:10,267 --> 00:06:16,233
Because many times when you don't have
the evidence or you don't have the metrics

96
00:06:16,233 --> 00:06:20,068
that are required, we end up saying
that, "Okay, yeah, this is the problem."

97
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:26,358
Or an agent may hallucinate and
assume or generate some mock

98
00:06:26,398 --> 00:06:28,261
data, and we don't want that.

99
00:06:28,664 --> 00:06:33,529
We want our incident agent to explicitly
call out when there's missing evidence.

100
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:39,765
And based on this too, on, for
a given model, a confidence

101
00:06:39,794 --> 00:06:41,017
moves the workflow state.

102
00:06:42,086 --> 00:06:46,779
But the authority always stays
with the operator, and the

103
00:06:46,779 --> 00:06:48,439
